/*  EXPECTED: REJECTED at type-check, identically by both backends.
    An object made in the rabbit holds a series from outside it; a rabbit's series is stored through the field.

    A name records where the NAME was made; the store is judged against where what it reaches
    was made, which can be further out. Judged once everything is checked, so a later statement
    that lowers it counts too (docs/SOUNDNESS.md, obligation O2). */

Define object bag with (the series of series of number items).
Define outer as a series of series of number.
Pull a rabbit.
    Define b as a new bag { the items outer }.
    Define inner as a series of number with (1, 2, 3).
    Insert inner into b's items.
Done.
State outer.
